[' I will provide an outline for a modular, asynchronous C# HTTP endpoint that meets your requirements. This solution uses Redis for caching and external content management service (CMS) integration.

1. Create an `UpdateEndpoint` class:

```csharp
public class UpdateEndpoint
{
    private readonly IRedisCache _redisCache;
    private readonly ICmsService _cmsService;
    // Other dependencies...

    public UpdateEndpoint(IRedisCache redisCache, ICmsService cmsService)
    {
        _redisCache = redisCache;
        _cmsService = cmsService;
    }

    [HttpPost]
    public async Task<IActionResult> ProcessUpdatesAsync([FromBody] BatchUpdateRequest request)
    {
        // Request validation and idempotency checks...

        var tasks = new List<Task>();

        foreach (var update in request.Updates)
        {
            tasks.Add(ProcessSingleUpdateAsync(update));
        }

        await Task.WhenAll(tasks);

        return Ok();
    }
}
```

2. Implement the `BatchUpdateRequest` and `SingleUpdate` models:

